<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shu Yu of Tang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> · Also known as Tang Shu Yu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shu Yu of Tang was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-wu-of-zhou">King Wu of Zhou</a> and younger brother of King Cheng, who received the fief of Tang in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shanxi">Shanxi</a> in the 11th century BCE. His son Xie renamed the state Jin, so Shu Yu is regarded as the founder of the State of Jin, which became one of the great powers of the Spring and Autumn period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shu-yu-of-tang.jpg" alt="Shu Yu of Tang" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gisling · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%99%8B%E7%A5%A0%E8%83%9C%E5%A2%83.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
